      "id": "a2cp1-p1",
      "type": "comprehension",
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "fromSection": "a2-02",
      "title": "Pas seserį",
      "passage": "Šiandien esu pas seserį. Ji mokosi istorijos ir niekada nesimoko be knygos. Rytais ji keliasi anksti, prausiasi ir nusišypso. „Kaip sekasi?“ — klausiu. „Gerai, tik nesijaučiu žvali dėl darbo,“ — sako ji. Vakare mes matomės su draugais šalia parko ir kalbame apie filmą. Aš laukiu autobuso, o ji ieško bilieto.",
      "translation": "Today I am at my sister's. She is studying history and never studies without a book. In the mornings she gets up early, washes and smiles. \"How are you getting on?\" I ask. \"Fine, only I do not feel lively because of work,\" she says. In the evening we meet with friends beside the park and talk about a film. I wait for the bus, and she looks for a ticket.",
      "glossary": {
        "žvali": "lively (fem.)"
      },
